    "created_at": "2016-11-10T04:33:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-11-10T04:33:36Z",
    "body": "For a given property on a given cross-origin object, we should mint a new property descriptor for each caller global, rather than each caller origin. So I think this spec change is correct.\n\nIs this in the tests? If not, it should be (two same-origin iframes accessing a cross-origin global, ensuring that they get different property descriptors).\n",
